          "start_line": 1446
        }
      ],
      "key": "occurrence_profile",
      "label": "Traversal-occurrence profile"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Complete specialization RefDomain_Sigma_occurrence(record_kind, qualified_field). O:S denotes semantic-object sort S; AnyLocal is exactly O union E union C union L union X union V union T union J; Sigma:K denotes one exact member of a closed signature population; an empty table cell supplies no target in that class. ReferenceDomain, ExternalTargetKind and BasisRelation are this profile's signature populations. B_model means the same M_occ,b and record basis; B_profile exact TraversalOccurrenceProfileBasis resolution; B_calculus exact imported AxiomaticCalculusBasis resolution; B_adopted the exact Product-adoption basis relation named for the external kind.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 263,
          "quote": "The basis codes are exact relations, not labels (P3):",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FClosed%20semantic-object%20sorts%2FFinite%20reference-domain%20table",
          "start_line": 247
        }
      ],
      "key": "reference_domain",
      "label": "Finite reference domain"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
